<h2>Triggers as Teachers</h2>
<p>Two flaggers, opposite directions, and one very loud teacher. A short true story about
reading your triggers as teachers &mdash; pause, name it, and stay for the lesson.</p>
<p>In my work I hold a distinction: <em>reacting to the trigger is bravery &mdash;
responding to the trigger is courage.</em> This walk is where that lesson was learned.</p>
